IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sssa-nouns`
IMPORT `sssa-part1-preliminary`
IMPORT `sssa-part2-scheme`
IMPORT `sssa-part3-administration`
IMPORT `sssa-part4-miscellaneous`
IMPORT `sssa-seat`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for the Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 (Singapore).
-- Every expected value comes from ANSWERS.md, written from the source text BEFORE any .l4 file was opened.
-- Numbers are the scenario numbers of ANSWERS.md ("S<n>" = the seat addendum).
-- A failing assertion is a finding: no expected value here was changed to match the encoding.
-- Tags: [R3] = a condition ("where", a stated manner, "who") fails and I expect FALSE, the family reading is NOTHING.
--       [R3b] = an element of an offence fails and I expect FALSE, the family reading is NOTHING.
--       (J) = a judgement call recorded as such in ANSWERS.md.
-- Items that cannot be asked of the encoding are GAPs and are listed in the report, not asserted.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Test helpers (record builders only; no rule)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN y IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      d IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Birth facts`
`t birth` MEANS `Birth facts` OF y, m, d

GIVEN isBoard IS A BOOLEAN
      isPO IS A BOOLEAN
      isPA IS A BOOLEAN
      appointed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Body asked about as an administrator`
`t admin body` MEANS `Body asked about as an administrator` OF isBoard, isPO, isPA, appointed

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person asked about as an investigator`
`t investigator` MEANS `Person asked about as an investigator` OF a, b

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Information asked about as means information`
`t info` MEANS `Information asked about as means information` OF a, b, c

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Body asked about as a public authority`
`t authority` MEANS `Body asked about as a public authority` OF a, b

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Scheme asked about as a public scheme`
`t scheme` MEANS `Scheme asked about as a public scheme` OF a, b, c, d, e, f

GIVEN officer IS A BOOLEAN
      authorised IS A BOOLEAN
      goodFaith IS A BOOLEAN
      care IS A BOOLEAN
      accesses IS A BOOLEAN
      discloses IS A BOOLEAN
      otherAuth IS A BOOLEAN
      meansInfo IS A BOOLEAN
      conf IS A BOOLEAN
      duties IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Conduct of an officer of an information recipient`
`t conduct` MEANS `Conduct of an officer of an information recipient` OF officer, authorised, goodFaith, care, accesses, discloses, otherAuth, meansInfo, conf, duties

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Use or disclosure asked about under section 9(2)`
`t use` MEANS `Use or disclosure asked about under section 9(2)` OF a, b, c, d

GIVEN c IS A STRING
      a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Class amount`
`t class` MEANS `Class amount` OF c, a

-- ===========================================================================
-- B. Interpretation, s 2
-- ===========================================================================

-- 31 s 2 administrator: the Board
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is an administrator` (`t admin body` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 32 s 2 administrator: a public officer appointed under s 5(4)
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is an administrator` (`t admin body` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 33 s 2 administrator: a public authority appointed under s 5(4)
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is an administrator` (`t admin body` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 34 s 2 administrator: a public officer not appointed
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is an administrator` (`t admin body` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 35 s 2 administrator: a public authority not appointed by the Minister under s 5(4)
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is an administrator` (`t admin body` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 36 s 2 Board: the CPF Board
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is the Board` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 37 s 2 Board: some other body (Housing and Development Board)
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is the Board` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 36b s 2 Board: not known whether the body is the CPF Board constituted under the CPF Act 1953 (R5)
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is the Board` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 38 s 2 cash grant: made by the Government under the Scheme
#ASSERT `s 2 the payment is a cash grant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 39 s 2 cash grant: made by a private charity (not the Government)
#ASSERT `s 2 the payment is a cash grant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 41 s 2 Commissioner: appointed under s 4(1)
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is the Commissioner` `appointed under section 4(1) as the Commissioner for Silver Support` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 42 s 2 Commissioner includes a Deputy Commissioner appointed under s 4(2)(a)
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is the Commissioner` `appointed under section 4(2)(a) as a Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 43 s 2 Commissioner includes an Assistant Commissioner appointed under s 4(2)(b)
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is the Commissioner` `appointed under section 4(2)(b) as an Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 44/45 s 2 Commissioner: an investigator, or a deputy not appointed by the Minister under s 4, is not within the definition
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is the Commissioner` `not appointed under section 4` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 46 s 2 eligible individual: an individual eligible for a benefit
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an eligible individual` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 47 s 2 eligible individual: a company is not an individual
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an eligible individual` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 48 s 2 investigator: a Board officer authorised under s 5(7)
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an investigator` (`t investigator` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 49 s 2 investigator: a person appointed under s 5(8)
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an investigator` (`t investigator` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 50 s 2 investigator: a Board officer not authorised
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is an investigator` (`t investigator` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 52 s 2 means information: income of an individual held by a Government department
#ASSERT `s 2 the information is means information` (`t info` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 53 s 2 means information: assets of a household held by a public authority
#ASSERT `s 2 the information is means information` (`t info` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 54 s 2 means information: health information is neither income nor assets
#ASSERT `s 2 the information is means information` (`t info` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 55 s 2 means information: income held only by a private bank
#ASSERT `s 2 the information is means information` (`t info` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 57 s 2 public authority: established by a public Act to perform a public function
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is a public authority` (`t authority` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 58 s 2 public authority: neither (a private charity trust)
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is a public authority` (`t authority` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 59 s 2 public authority: established by a public Act but with no public function
#ASSERT `s 2 the body is a public authority` (`t authority` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 60 s 2 public scheme: written law, administered by the Government, supports citizens
#ASSERT `s 2 the scheme is a public scheme` (`t scheme` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 61 s 2 public scheme: supports permanent residents only
#ASSERT `s 2 the scheme is a public scheme` (`t scheme` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 62 s 2 public scheme: supports foreigners only (neither citizens nor permanent residents)
#ASSERT `s 2 the scheme is a public scheme` (`t scheme` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 63 s 2 public scheme: not established by or under written law
#ASSERT `s 2 the scheme is a public scheme` (`t scheme` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 64 s 2 public scheme: under written law but administered by a private company
#ASSERT `s 2 the scheme is a public scheme` (`t scheme` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 66 s 2 public scheme: supports a part of the citizens only
#ASSERT `s 2 the scheme is a public scheme` (`t scheme` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 67 s 2 permanent resident: the Immigration Act 1959 decides, so an unknown status is not covered (R5)
#ASSERT `s 2 the person is a permanent resident of Singapore` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 68 s 2 Scheme: the Silver Support Scheme under s 5(1)
#ASSERT `s 2 the scheme is the Scheme` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 69 s 2 Scheme: any other scheme
#ASSERT `s 2 the scheme is the Scheme` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 460 s 2 chapeau: where the context otherwise requires, the definitions do not apply ("unless")
#ASSERT `s 2 the definitions apply to the term as used` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 461 s 2 chapeau: where the context does not otherwise require, the definitions apply
#ASSERT `s 2 the definitions apply to the term as used` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- ===========================================================================
-- D. Part 2: ss 5, 6, 7
-- ===========================================================================

-- 88 s 5(1) the Scheme is known as the Silver Support Scheme
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the name by which the established scheme is known` EQUALS "Silver Support Scheme"
-- 88b s 5(1) the purpose is providing financial support to eligible individuals
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the purpose for which the Scheme is established` EQUALS "providing financial support to eligible individuals"

-- 112 s 6(1) eligible: citizen, attained 65 on the day asked, other criteria met
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 113 s 6(1)(a) not a citizen (a 70-year-old permanent resident)
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` FALSE (`t birth` (JUST 1955) (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 114 s 6(1)(b) a citizen aged 64
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`t birth` (JUST 1961) (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 115 s 6(1)(c) the prescribed criteria are not met
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`t birth` (JUST 1955) (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 116 s 6(1)(c) the prescribed criteria are in regulations outside the text (R5)
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`t birth` (JUST 1955) (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 117 s 6(1) before s 6 commenced (22 July 2016): a citizen aged 76 is not yet an eligible individual (J)
-- GAP 2026-11-04 117: not asserted. The reviewer wrote `#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`t birth` (JUST 1940) (JUST 5) (JUST 5)) (Date 21 7 2016) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE` (expected JUST FALSE: a citizen aged 76, asked about 21 July 2016, before s 6 commenced on 22 July 2016). The encoding models no commencement date, so it answers JUST TRUE; that answer is not blessed by any assertion. See NOTES.md finding 24.
-- 118 s 6(1) on the commencement day itself
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`t birth` (JUST 1940) (JUST 5) (JUST 5)) (Date 22 7 2016) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 119 s 6(1) a non-citizen under 65
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` FALSE (`t birth` (JUST 1990) (JUST 1) (JUST 1)) (Date 15 3 2025) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===========================================================================
-- E. Age and time counting, s 6(2)
-- ===========================================================================

-- 121 s 6(2)(a) born 1960-03-15 attains 65 on 2025-03-15
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2025)
-- 122 s 6(1)(b) has not attained 65 on 2025-03-14
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 123 s 6(1)(b) has attained 65 on the 65th anniversary itself
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 124 s 6(1)(b) has attained 65 the day after
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 126 s 6(2)(b) born on 29 February 1960: the 65th anniversary is deemed to be 1 March 2025
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 2) (JUST 29)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)
-- 127 s 6(2)(b) born 1960-02-29: not yet 65 on 2025-02-28
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 2) (JUST 29)) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 128 s 6(2)(b) born 1960-02-29: 65 on 2025-03-01
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 2) (JUST 29)) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 129 s 6(2)(b) born 1964-02-29 attains 65 on 2029-03-01
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1964) (JUST 2) (JUST 29)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2029)
-- 130 s 6(2)(b) born 2000-02-29 attains 65 on 2065-03-01
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 2000) (JUST 2) (JUST 29)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2065)
-- 131 s 6(2)(b) born 1948-02-29 attains 65 on 2013-03-01
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1948) (JUST 2) (JUST 29)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2013)
-- 132 s 6(2)(a) born 28 February: no leap-day rule, 65 on 2025-02-28
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 2) (JUST 28)) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- 133 s 6(2)(a) born 1 March attains 65 on 2025-03-01
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 3) (JUST 1)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)
-- 134 s 6(2)(a) born on the 31st (31 August) attains 65 on 2025-08-31
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 8) (JUST 31)) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 8 2025)
-- 135a s 6(1)(b) born 1960-12-31: not 65 on 2025-12-30
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 12) (JUST 31)) (Date 30 12 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 135b s 6(1)(b) born 1960-12-31: 65 on 2025-12-31
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 12) (JUST 31)) (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 137 s 6(2)(c) day not ascertained, March 1960: deemed born 1 March, attains 65 on 2025-03-01
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 3) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)
-- 138a s 6(2)(c) day not ascertained, March 1960: not 65 on 2025-02-28
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 3) NOTHING) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 138b s 6(2)(c) day not ascertained, March 1960: 65 on 2025-03-01
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 3) NOTHING) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 139 s 6(2)(c) day not ascertained, February 1960: deemed 1 February, 65 on 2025-02-01
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 2) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 2 2025)
-- 140 s 6(2)(c) day not ascertained, January 1960: 65 on 2025-01-01
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) (JUST 1) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2025)
-- 141 s 6(2)(d) month not ascertained but day known (17th): deemed January, 65 on 2025-01-17 (J)
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) NOTHING (JUST 17)) EQUALS JUST (Date 17 1 2025)
-- 142 s 6(2)(c)+(d) month and day not ascertained: 1 January, 65 on 2025-01-01 (J)
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` (JUST 1960) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2025)
-- 143 s 6(2) year not ascertained: the text is silent
#ASSERT `s 6(2)(a) the date on which the individual attains 65 years of age` (`t birth` NOTHING (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 143b s 6(1)(b) year not ascertained: no answer
#ASSERT `s 6(1)(b) the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`t birth` NOTHING (JUST 3) (JUST 15)) (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 144 s 6(1) born 1951-07-22, a citizen: eligible on 2016-07-22 (65th birthday = commencement day)
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`t birth` (JUST 1951) (JUST 7) (JUST 22)) (Date 22 7 2016) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 145 s 6(1) born 1951-07-23: not eligible on 2016-07-22
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`t birth` (JUST 1951) (JUST 7) (JUST 23)) (Date 22 7 2016) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 146 s 6(1) born 1951-07-23: eligible on 2016-07-23
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the individual is an eligible individual` TRUE (`t birth` (JUST 1951) (JUST 7) (JUST 23)) (Date 23 7 2016) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- ===========================================================================
-- F. Benefits, s 7
-- ===========================================================================

-- 153 s 7(1) an eligible individual is eligible for the benefits prescribed
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be prescribed` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 154 s 7(1) the amount is in regulations outside the text (R5)
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the amount of benefit an eligible individual is eligible to receive` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 154b s 7(1) the amount, when the caller supplies the prescribed 600
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the amount of benefit an eligible individual is eligible to receive` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 600) EQUALS JUST 600
-- 155 s 7(2) different amounts for different classes: the class table returns the prescribed amount
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the amount prescribed for the class of eligible individual` "B" (LIST (`t class` "A" 100), (`t class` "B" 200)) EQUALS JUST 200
-- 156 s 7(2) no regulations supplied (empty table): not covered (R5)
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the amount prescribed for the class of eligible individual` "A" EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- 158 s 7(1) the manner of payment is prescribed (R5)
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the manner in which an eligible individual is to receive the benefit` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 159 s 7(1) a person who is not an eligible individual: the grant says nothing of them
#ASSERT `s 7(1) the individual is eligible to receive the benefits that may be prescribed` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

