-- GAPS ADDED 2026-11-04 (not assertions). The independent test author wrote 173 numbered scenarios in its ANSWERS.md (not shipped) that it did not turn into
-- assertions, because the encoding has no function for the question, or its function has no input for the distinguishing fact (about 17 of them repeat a call it had already asserted).
-- Each line is the author's own wording from ANSWERS.md, shortened at 400 characters; the scenario number is the author's. Nothing below is run.
-- Answer key of the author: Y = yes / TRUE; N = no / FALSE; NC = not covered; (J) = a judgement call. Its rule R3 counted a failed 'if', 'where' or stated-manner condition as N.
