-- GAP 26: Is the Act still in force on 2030-01-01? => NC (consolidation stops at 1/12/2025; no sunset clause).
-- GAP 27: Does the Act contain a sunset or expiry date? => NC (R6).
-- GAP 28: Do benefits paid before 2016-07-22 remain valid after s 6 and s 7 commence (transitional)? => NC (no savings clause).
-- GAP 29: If a repealed provision were revived, from when would it apply? => NC (no revival clause).
-- GAP 30: L146-148, s 3: does s 3 itself confer an entitlement to payment on an elderly citizen? => NC (a statement of purpose; no operative words).
-- GAP 40: A cash grant disbursed by the Board on behalf of the Government under s 5(2) is a "cash grant" => Y (J: s 5(2) says the Board acts on behalf of the Government).
-- GAP 51: A public officer authorised by the Commissioner to investigate is an investigator => N (s 5(7) authorisation is by the Board, and only of Board officers or employees; R1).
-- GAP 56: The Board is a "public authority" => Y (J: the text never says so directly, but s 5(4), s 8(7)(e), s 9(1) and s 19(3) say "public authority (other than the Board)", which only makes sense if the Board is one).
