-- GAP 76: s 4(2)(a): the Minister, in writing, appoints an employee of a public authority as a Deputy Commissioner => Y.
-- GAP 77: s 4(2)(b): the Minister, in writing, appoints an employee of a public authority as an Assistant Commissioner => Y.
-- GAP 78: s 4(2): the Minister appoints a Deputy Commissioner orally => N (R3).
-- GAP 79: s 4(2): maximum number of Deputy Commissioners => NC (no cap stated).
-- GAP 80: s 4(1): can the Minister revoke an appointment, and its term => NC.
-- GAP 81: s 4(3): the Commissioner for Silver Support is responsible for the administration of the Act => Y.
-- GAP 82: s 4(3): a Deputy Commissioner (as such) is responsible for the administration of the Act => N (J: s 4(3) puts responsibility on "the Commissioner for Silver Support"; a Deputy only performs functions under s 4(4)).
-- GAP 83: s 4(4): a Deputy Commissioner may perform the Commissioner's functions and exercise the Commissioner's powers => Y.
-- GAP 84: s 4(4): an Assistant Commissioner may do so => Y.
-- GAP 85: s 4(4): a Deputy may exercise a power the Commissioner has directed him not to exercise => N ("subject to the directions").
-- GAP 86: s 4(4): a Deputy may exercise the Commissioner's powers when the Commissioner has given no direction => Y.
-- GAP 87: s 5(1): the Scheme is established on 2016-01-18 => Y; on 2016-01-17 => N.
-- GAP 89: s 5(2): the Board administers the Scheme and enforces the Act on behalf of the Government => Y (a duty: "is to").
-- GAP 90: s 5(2): the Board administers the Scheme against a direction of the Commissioner => N ("subject to the directions").
-- GAP 91: s 5(3)(a): where the Board administers the Scheme, the CPF Act 1953 provisions apply to the Board in respect of that administration => Y.
-- GAP 92: s 5(3)(b): a Board employee, in relation to administering the Scheme, is deemed a public officer for the Financial Procedure Act 1966 => Y.
-- GAP 93: s 5(3)(b): the deeming applies to a Board employee in respect of CPF work wholly unrelated to the Scheme => N (R3: "in relation to their administration of the Scheme and enforcement of this Act").
-- GAP 94: s 5(3)(b): the deeming applies even if the employee was never employed by the Government => Y ("even though ...").
-- GAP 95: s 5(4): the Minister may appoint a public officer to assist the Board in administering the Scheme => Y.
-- GAP 96: s 5(4): the Minister may appoint a public authority (other than the Board) to assist the Board => Y.
-- GAP 97: s 5(4): the Minister may appoint the Board itself under s 5(4) => N (L214-215 "other than the Board").
-- GAP 98: s 5(4): the Minister may appoint a private company under s 5(4) => NC (R4).
-- GAP 99: s 5(4): an appointee may assist in ways other than disbursing or conferring benefits => Y ("for instance" is illustrative).
-- GAP 100: s 5(5): the Minister must publish in the Gazette a notice of the appointment of a public authority appointed under s 5(4) => Y (a duty).
-- GAP 101: s 5(5): the notice must be published within 7 days => NC ("as soon as practicable" gives no number of days).
-- GAP 102: s 5(5): an appointment that is not gazetted is void => NC.
-- GAP 103: s 5(5): the Minister must gazette an appointment of an investigator under s 5(8) => NC (the duty is limited to s 5(4) appointments; R4).
-- GAP 104: s 5(6)(a): where a public authority is appointed under s 5(4), its functions under written law are regarded as including administering the Scheme => Y.
-- GAP 105: s 5(6)(b): that authority is regarded as fulfilling the purposes of the Act that constitutes it => Y.
-- GAP 106: s 5(6)(c): its members, officers and employees are deemed public officers for the Financial Procedure Act 1966 => Y.
-- GAP 107: s 5(6): the same consequences apply where a public OFFICER (not an authority) is appointed under s 5(4) => N (R3: "where a public authority is appointed").
-- GAP 108: s 5(7): the Board may authorise a Board employee to conduct an investigation => Y.
-- GAP 109: s 5(7): the Board may authorise a non-Board public officer under s 5(7) => NC (R4).
-- GAP 110: s 5(8): the Minister may in writing appoint any person (including a private person) to assist the Board in an investigation => Y.
-- GAP 111: s 5(8): the same appointment made orally => N (R3).
-- GAP 120: s 3 (L146-148): does the purpose clause make a 70-year-old permanent resident eligible? => N (s 3 does not override s 6).
-- GAP 125: Born 1960-03-15: attained 65 at 00:00 on 2025-03-15 (any moment of the anniversary day) => Y (s 6(2)(a): attains "on the 65th anniversary"; the text counts days, not hours).
-- GAP 136: Born 1960-02-29: the date on which this person attains 21 (1981-02-29 does not exist) => NC (s 6(2)(b) deals only with the 65th anniversary).
-- GAP 147: Which day is "the last day" of a period of years: the 65th anniversary is the day on which age 65 is attained, not the day after => Y (s 6(2)(a)).
-- GAP 148: A period of 14 days under this Act that begins on 2025-01-31: the last day => NC (R6).
-- GAP 149: A period of one month that begins on 2025-01-31: the last day => NC (R6; no month-end rule).
-- GAP 150: A period that ends on a Sunday or public holiday: does it extend to the next working day? => NC (R6).
-- GAP 151: A period of 2 weeks that begins on 2025-02-28: the last day => NC (R6).
-- GAP 152: A period that begins on 2024-02-29 and runs one year: the last day => NC (R6).
-- GAP 157: s 7(2): regulations may prescribe different methods of disbursing benefits for different classes => Y.
-- GAP 162: s 8(1): there is no certification at all => N.
-- GAP 163: s 8(1): the certification is made by the Commissioner, not the Minister => N (R3: the condition names "the Minister").
-- GAP 165: s 8(1)(a): a different Minister (not the one charged with the department) gives the direction => NC (R4).
-- GAP 166: s 8(1)(a): the s 8(1)(a) power is "in addition to" other powers: the existence of another statutory power to obtain the information does not remove it => Y.
-- GAP 178: s 8(3): the same, access at exactly time T (the moment of notification) => N ("from the time ... is notified").
-- GAP 183: s 8(3): the prohibition applies to a person who is not an authorised person => NC (R4).
-- GAP 196: s 8(4)(b): the protection requires BOTH good faith AND reasonable care ("and") => Y (so having one only is not enough).
-- GAP 198: s 8(5): the Commissioner may attach terms to a direction given by the Minister => NC (R4).
-- GAP 205: s 8(6): a minimum penalty => NC.
-- GAP 206: s 8(6): intent is required for the offence => NC (the text says "any act in contravention").
-- GAP 217: s 8(7) "officer" (b): an employee of the same authority NOT acting under his direction => N.
-- GAP 238: s 9(3)(b): the report may include additional information beyond (i) and (ii) => NC.
-- GAP 239: s 9(3)(b)(ii): benefits received on the very day the report is made are included ("up to the date on which the report is made") => NC (genuine ambiguity; "up to" does not say whether the date is included).
-- GAP 243: s 9(4): the Commissioner may attach terms to the Minister's approval => NC (R4).
-- GAP 251: s 9(6): obtained on 2016-01-18 => Y; obtained on 2016-01-19 => Y.
-- GAP 254: s 9(6): the use requires the individual's consent => NC (the clause states none).
-- GAP 263: s 10(1): underpayment ($100 short): the Government must pay the shortfall => NC.
-- GAP 267: s 10(1): the grant was paid to a third party who is not "the recipient" => NC.
-- GAP 269: s 10(2)(a): by a reckless false statement => Y.
-- GAP 271: s 10(2)(a): a misleading statement that is literally true => Y ("false or misleading").
-- GAP 273: s 10(2)(b): a document the individual ought reasonably to know is false in a material particular => Y.
-- GAP 274: s 10(2)(b): a document false only in an immaterial particular => N.
-- GAP 275: s 10(2)(b): a document the individual neither knew nor ought reasonably to know was false => N.
-- GAP 277: s 10(2): dishonest intention is required => N (that is s 11, not s 10(2)).
-- GAP 278: s 10(2): benefit obtained was an "other benefit" (not cash): recoverable => Y.
-- GAP 279: s 10(2): how an in-kind benefit is valued => NC.
-- GAP 280: s 10(2): who bears the burden of proof => NC.
-- GAP 285: s 10(3): a cap on the part of the cash grant that may be set off => NC.
-- GAP 286: s 10(3): set-off against the recipient's private bank account => NC.
-- GAP 290: s 11(1): attempt to obtain (nothing obtained): liable under s 11 => NC (attempt is not addressed here).
-- GAP 294: s 11(1): the person dishonestly obtains the grant for another person => NC.
-- GAP 295: s 11(1): aiding or abetting => NC.
-- GAP 297: s 11(2): a conviction under s 11 extinguishes the right of recovery under s 10 => N (s 11(2): "does not affect").
-- GAP 300: s 12: the court MUST make the order => N ("may").
-- GAP 302: s 12: the order is for the amount certified by the administrator as recoverable as at the date of conviction => Y.
-- GAP 303: s 12: the court orders more than the certified amount => N.
-- GAP 307: s 12: the order is made in addition to the penalty => Y.
-- GAP 308: s 12: the court may make the order INSTEAD of imposing any penalty => NC.
-- GAP 311: s 13: the certificate is conclusive evidence => N ("prima facie").
-- GAP 313: s 13: applies in proceedings before a court, a tribunal or an authority => Y.
-- GAP 314: s 13: applies in criminal proceedings => Y ("any proceedings").
-- GAP 317: s 13: the evidence extends to the amount at a later date than the certified date => NC.
-- GAP 318: s 13: the certificate shifts the burden of proof to the accused => NC.
-- GAP 320: s 14(1): a Deputy Commissioner may do so => Y (included in "Commissioner").
-- GAP 325: s 14(1)(a): the notice may require a signed written statement => Y.
-- GAP 328: s 14(1)(b)(i): the information is not within the person's knowledge => N.
-- GAP 329: s 14(1)(b)(ii): the document is not in the person's possession => N.
-- GAP 332: s 14(1)(c): the Commissioner may make copies or extracts without payment => Y.
-- GAP 333: s 14(1)(c): the Commissioner must pay the holder for the copies => N ("without payment").
-- GAP 334: s 14(1)(c): how long the original may be retained => NC.
-- GAP 337: s 14(2): the Commissioner may require the file in its native format => NC.
-- GAP 341: s 14(3): a copy NOT certified => NC.
-- GAP 348: s 14(4): the minimum time that must be allowed => NC.
-- GAP 349: s 14: deemed service of the written notice: a notice posted on 2025-06-01 is deemed served on a date => NC (R6).
-- GAP 351: s 15: the person obstructs a Deputy Commissioner => Y.
-- GAP 357: s 15: intent is required => NC.
-- GAP 363: s 16(1): the offence is not one under this Act (a Penal Code offence) => N.
-- GAP 365: s 16(1): the officer is liable even if the body corporate is not prosecuted => NC.
-- GAP 366: s 16(1): the body corporate is also guilty ("as well as") => Y.
-- GAP 402: s 17(1): an offence under another Act may be compounded under s 17 => N ("any offence under this Act").
-- GAP 404: s 17(2): once the company has paid, proceedings against its director under s 16 for the same offence => NC (the bar is on proceedings against "that person").
-- GAP 405: s 17(2): a partial payment bars proceedings => NC.
-- GAP 407: s 17(3): the Board may keep the sum => N.
-- GAP 412: s 18: the offence is under another Act => N.
-- GAP 413: s 18: the Public Prosecutor may no longer conduct the proceedings himself => NC.
-- GAP 418: s 19(1): "purported execution" counts: an act done under a defective authority => Y (protected).
-- GAP 419: s 19(1): an omission => Y (protected).
-- GAP 421: s 19(1): the protection removes the Government's own liability => NC ("personally").
-- GAP 424: s 19(3): the public authority itself, as a legal entity => NC.
-- GAP 429: s 20(1): the Commissioner may make regulations => NC (R4).
-- GAP 438: s 20(2)(h): fees for a matter where the Minister thinks it NOT expedient => N.
-- GAP 440: s 20(2)(i): on compoundable offences under s 17(1) => Y.
-- GAP 444: s 20(3): regulations MUST create an offence => N ("may").
-- GAP 445: s 20(4): regulations must be presented to Parliament as soon as possible after publication in the Gazette => Y.
-- GAP 446: s 20(4): the number of days allowed for presenting them => NC.
-- GAP 447: s 20(4): regulations lapse if not presented => NC.
-- GAP 448: s 20(4): Parliament must approve the regulations before they take effect => NC.
-- GAP 449: s 20: the commencement date of regulations => NC.
-- GAP 450: If the Central Provident Fund Act 1953 is repealed and re-enacted, does a reference to "section 3 of the Central Provident Fund Act 1953" in s 2 continue to refer to the new section? => NC (R6).
-- GAP 451: If s 20 of the Financial Procedure Act 1966 is amended, does s 5(3)(b) follow the amended text? => NC.
-- GAP 452: If the Immigration Act 1959 s 2 is replaced, does "permanent resident of Singapore" follow? => NC.
-- GAP 453: Are regulations made under s 20 void if inconsistent with the Act? => NC.
-- GAP 454: Does the Act bind the Government? => NC.
-- GAP 455: Is there a right of appeal against an assessment of eligibility? => NC (only regulations on review, s 20(2)(e)).
-- GAP 456: Is the benefit assignable or exempt from attachment? => NC.
-- GAP 457: Is there a limitation period for prosecuting offences? => NC.
-- GAP 458: Can a deceased person's estate be pursued under s 10? => NC.
-- GAP 459: Is the Minister required to give reasons for refusing an approval under s 9(3)(a)? => NC.
